      "description": "Watch Fiorentina vs Pisa highlights and goals from Coppa Italia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 15, 2026. On September 15, 2026, the Coppa Italia took center stage as Fiorentina hosted Pisa in a knockout encounter filled with tactical intrigue. Both sets of supporters arrived at the stadium expecting a fierce battle for supremacy in one of Italy’s most prestigious cup competitions. Pellegrino Breaks the Deadlock The match began with high intensity, as both teams fought for control in the central areas. Early disciplinary issues saw Franco Mastantuono booked just six minutes into the game, setting a physical tone. As the first half progressed, Pisa struggled to contain the home side's growing pressure. The breakthrough finally arrived in the 40th minute when Mateo Pellegrino found the back of the net, rewarding Fiorentina 's persistence and sending them into the half-time break with a vital lead. Second Half Adjustments and Momentum The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to influence the outcome. Fiorentina introduced Viery for Radu Dragusin immediately after the restart, while a flurry of substitutions around the hour mark brought fresh energy to the pitch. The introduction of Alieu Njie and Pedro Gonçalves proved to be a masterstroke, as the home side tightened their grip on the match. Despite yellow cards for Simone Canestrelli and Victor Valdepenas , the flow of the game remained firmly in the hands of the hosts. Sealing the Victory In the 71st minute, the pressure told once again. Wilfried Gnonto doubled the lead with a clinical finish, expertly assisted by Alieu Njie . As the clock ticked towards full-time, Pisa found it difficult to muster a comeback against a disciplined defensive line. The scoring was completed in stoppage time when Pedro Gonçalves netted a third goal in the 90+2nd minute, courtesy of an Alex Jimenez assist. The referee's final whistle confirmed a comprehensive 3-0 victory, ensuring Fiorentina 's progression to the next round."
